# React Patterns

## Container / Presentational

Containers own data/side effects; presentational components render from props. With App Router, Server Components often play the container role and pass data into Client Components.

## State Location

1. One component → `useState`
2. Parent + few children → lift + props
3. Distant low-frequency → Context
4. Shareable URL state → **nuqs**
5. Server-derived portfolio data → **tRPC** (TanStack Query on the client)

## Suspense + Errors

Pair every Suspense boundary with `ErrorBoundary` from `@/components/error-boundary` (`react-error-boundary`). Prefer narrow boundaries; compose child `skeleton.tsx` files instead of one giant parent skeleton (see `21-file-organization.mdc`).

```tsx
import { Suspense } from "react"
import { ErrorBoundary } from "@/components/error-boundary"
import { WorksList } from "./_components/works-list"
import { WorksListSkeleton } from "./_components/works-list/skeleton"

<ErrorBoundary>
  <Suspense fallback={<WorksListSkeleton />}>
    <WorksList />
  </Suspense>
</ErrorBoundary>
```


## Forms

Use **TanStack Form** + **Zod** for all non-trivial forms (see `20-portfolio-stack.mdc`). Prefer uncontrolled form actions only for trivial one-field cases.

## Data Fetching

| Strategy | When |
|---|---|
| tRPC in Server Components / routers | Default for portfolio works and mutations |
| TanStack Query via tRPC client hooks | Client cache, optimistic UI, polling |
| RSC `await` of a tRPC caller | Server-rendered pages without client cache |
| `fetch` in `useEffect` | Avoid |

## Lists and Keys

Stable keys — never index for lists that reorder/insert/delete.

## Composition

Prefer `children`, slots, and compound components over inheritance.

## Animation

Use **GSAP** for intentional motion (see stack rule). Prefer a small number of purposeful animations over decorative noise.
